# Base image for every FROM in infrastructure/docker/Dockerfile (CONTRACT-DECISIONS item 20): the website's current pin,
# a Docker Official Image python:<version>-slim-trixie (CPython on Debian 13), by index digest (an index is the one
# entry that lists every platform). The tag beside the digest is documentation; Docker resolves the digest. ci.yml fails
# when any FROM that is not an earlier stage differs from BASE_IMAGE@BASE_DIGEST, so the two cannot drift. Plain shell
# assignments, read by /bin/sh.
# The website's lab-image/versions.env is the source of truth. .github/workflows/base-update.yml compares this file with
# it once a day and, when they differ, opens a pull request that moves the three values below and every FROM together
# (scripts/follow_website_base.py). The move is automatic, so this comment does not name a version: the values below
# are the truth, and `git log` on this file shows when it moved. Dependabot does not bump this base, because it follows
# the website's pin: .github/dependabot.yml has no docker entry.
BASE_IMAGE=python:3.15.2-slim-trixie
BASE_DIGEST=sha256:8c13a3f37a6a5b71498228e902c4b9f51c1f7900d49fabf71f9a650c6120e0d0
BASE_PYTHON_VERSION=3.15.2
